1
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:12,040
=Fatal Proximity to Him=

2
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:14,080
=Episode 4=

3
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:15,480
(Next stop:)

4
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:17,120
(Dongting Lake.)

5
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:18,720
(Passengers getting off...)

6
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:19,760
(I'm back on the bus again.)

7
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:21,840
(So I really am trapped in a loop.)

8
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:25,200
(Those dreams really happened.)

9
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:26,320
(Wait.)

10
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:28,960
(He Lan made enemies by running
with the wrong crowd)

11
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,160
(because he got close to me,)

12
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:32,960
(and the ER incident made everyone
know about us.)

13
00:00:33,160 --> 00:00:34,760
(His enemies thought
I was his girlfriend,)

14
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:35,920
(so they killed me.)

15
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:37,880
(So were all those horrible deaths)

16
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:39,840
(in my previous loops caused by He Lan?)

17
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:40,880
(Yes.)

18
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:43,480
(Otherwise, why would anyone
try to kill someone like me,)

19
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:45,680
(a mere harmless, ordinary girl?)

20
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:48,120
(All of it makes sense now.)

21
00:00:59,440 --> 00:00:59,880
Hey.

22
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:02,280
You're the one who

23
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:03,920
got beaten up like a pig in the rain

24
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:05,680
and I gave you a strawberry cake, right?

25
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:08,200
I heard

26
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:09,600
you're from No. 3 High School.

27
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:11,320
You transferred to our class today.

28
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,440
(Let's save time.)

29
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:18,040
(I need to recharge, after all.)

30
00:01:27,880 --> 00:01:28,920
(Today's Special:
Signature Strawberry Cake: 20 Yuan Each)

31
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:29,720
Aren't you buying one?

32
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:32,240
This is your favorite strawberry cake.

33
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:33,440
I...

34
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:42,880
(20 Yuan)
Is this because I gave you

35
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:43,960
a strawberry cake on that rainy day,

36
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:44,920
and now you want to pay me back?

37
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:46,440
You really don't have to.

38
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:47,560
As dancers,

39
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,680
we have strict weight requirements.

40
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,640
Too many sweets
will make me gain weight.

41
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:51,520
So...

42
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:52,720
I appreciate the thought.

43
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:58,880
(Next,)

44
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,040
(I'm going to make you all)

45
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:02,960
(pay for everything I've suffered.)

46
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:07,120
Are you sure they went inside?

47
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:08,480
I didn't see her go in.

48
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:09,600
She can't take PE,

49
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:11,720
so she must be hiding here to rest.

50
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:16,040
You two make a great couple.

51
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:17,560
The staff will open the door
tomorrow morning.

52
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:19,640
Give me the crutch!

53
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,000
Come on, give it to me!

54
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,120
Hand it over!

55
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,440
(Sorry, Zhang Jinghang.)

56
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:27,320
(If I give it to you,
you'll knock me out.)

57
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:48,240
What are you doing?

58
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:51,800
I'm helping the cleaner tidy up.

59
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,000
Make sure you get the job done.

60
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:11,320
Alright, everyone, that's all for today.

61
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:11,880
Class dismissed.

62
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:13,000
Fake being sick now.

63
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:13,600
I'll ask for leave.

64
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:14,480
Wait.

65
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:16,040
Not yet. Wait.

66
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:17,640
If I don't go now, it'll be too late.

67
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,880
Good things happen to good people.

68
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:22,120
Everyone,

69
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:24,600
there's a notice on the bulletin board.
Power repairs are scheduled tonight,

70
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,160
so evening study hall is canceled.

71
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:28,640
(- Wow!
- That's great!)

72
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:31,720
Did you secretly learn fortune-telling?

73
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:33,480
How did you know?

74
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:36,080
Hands on the floor.

75
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,080
Keep your hips square.

76
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:39,320
Turn your front leg outward.

77
00:03:39,920 --> 00:03:40,720
Point your toes.

78
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,840
(What if he got beaten to death?)

79
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:44,920
(Should I go save him?)

80
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:47,680
(If I don't go and he gets beaten
to death,)

81
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:49,400
(I won't survive either.)

82
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:54,840
Is this emergency service?

83
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:57,080
There's a fight at a billiards hall
on Fuxu Road.

84
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:00,400
(Guan Ying Billiards & Games Club)

85
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:08,640
(SO.T Xutai Esports Club
Guan Ying Billiards & Games Club)

86
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:14,640
Why are you here?

87
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:17,360
I was just passing by.

88
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:20,720
The wound on your back...

89
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:23,040
Oh,

90
00:04:23,760 --> 00:04:24,240
it's nothing.

91
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:26,120
There was trouble at the pool hall.

92
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:27,080
But someone called the police.

93
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:29,360
They all ran when they heard the sirens.

94
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:31,520
I was lucky.

95
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:33,120
Otherwise, it might've been worse
than a minor injury.

96
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:34,360
A minor injury?

97
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,440
How is this a minor injury?

98
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:38,960
Let's go to the hospital.

99
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,760
The cut is pretty long,

100
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,120
but luckily it's not deep.

101
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,040
No muscle damage.

102
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:50,040
I'll give you a tetanus shot.

103
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:16,960
Bear with it.

104
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:24,880
You're so good at studying.

105
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:26,640
Why get mixed up with gangs?

106
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:29,640
You're always getting new injuries
on top of old ones.

107
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:31,560
The money is quick.

108
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,440
(You get money fast,)

109
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:34,840
(but make enemies,)

110
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:36,240
(and I'm the one who gets killed.)

111
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:39,000
So you're living every day
like it's a battlefield.

112
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:40,800
Look at that huge scar on your back.

113
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:42,760
Once it heals,
it'll look like a centipede.

114
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:45,360
And whenever the seasons change,

115
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:46,960
it'll probably start hurting again.

116
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,560
Are you worried about me?

117
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,240
No, I'm not.

118
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:57,280
I'm just worried that next time I dance,

119
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,280
I won't have a good helper.

120
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:04,080
As long as you keep going
to the dance studio,

121
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:05,920
Song Shuqi

122
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,800
will definitely run into you again.

123
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:10,840
What if your mom

124
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,400
finds out again?

125
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:13,960
I'll take one step at a time.

126
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:15,760
There will always be a way.

127
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:19,160
Why do you love dancing so much?

128
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,320
Because

129
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:25,600
dancing makes me incredibly happy.

130
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:26,400
I can

131
00:06:26,960 --> 00:06:28,960
completely lose myself
in the world of dance.

132
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,160
Is there anything that makes you feel

133
00:06:35,640 --> 00:06:36,920
incredibly happy?

134
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:00,800
He Lan?

135
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:01,720
Come on in!

136
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:02,320
Hello, Ms. Luo.

137
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:03,440
I'm here to take

138
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:04,560
Xiyu to make up her math lessons.

139
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:08,000
Then

140
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:08,880
come on in.

141
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,000
I won't go inside.

142
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:11,160
We'll go to the library.

143
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:12,320
It has a better study atmosphere.

144
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:12,920
Right.

145
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,440
I still have lots of math questions
to ask He Lan.

146
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:17,560
Can you teach me more from now on?

147
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,040
I'll try my best.

148
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:22,800
Studying at home is better.

149
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,480
Why keep running back and forth
to the library?

150
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:25,400
Come inside.

151
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,000
Ms. Luo,

152
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,840
you're usually busy with work.

153
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:29,760
If Xiyu and I are alone at home,

154
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:30,960
it might not be appropriate.

155
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:33,760
Makes sense.

156
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:35,600
I'll get my schoolbag, Mom.

157
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:40,960
You really know what to say.

158
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:42,440
You even won my mom over.

159
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:45,320
Sorry.

160
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:46,200
I didn't mean to.

161
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:47,400
I forgot you were injured.

162
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:50,280
I'll take you somewhere

163
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,880
where Song Shuqi won't bother you
while you dance.

164
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:53,520
Where?

165
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:55,120
Somewhere really good.

166
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:59,640
(Guan Ying Billiards & Games Club - 1F)

167
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:07,200
Well...

168
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:10,320
Won't your boss get mad?

169
00:08:10,560 --> 00:08:12,280
We don't open until 3:30 p.m.

170
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,040
The place isn't perfect,

171
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:15,560
but you can make do here.

172
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:18,600
Good.

173
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:19,320
Open.

174
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:20,560
Okay.

175
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:23,880
Very good.

176
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:25,040
Extend.

177
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,280
Rise.

178
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:28,600
Beautiful insteps.

179
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:31,520
Good.

180
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:33,720
Put some emotion into it.

181
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:41,000
(Mom)

182
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:44,920
I knew my mom wouldn't let this slide.

183
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,320
It's okay.

184
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:48,240
I was prepared.

185
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:49,400
Huh?

186
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:53,080
Mom,

187
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:53,960
what's wrong?

188
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:55,360
Xiyu,

189
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,360
how's your studying going?

190
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,560
It's great.

191
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:00,880
This whole afternoon,

192
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:01,640
He Lan

193
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:03,280
taught me several math problems.

194
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,560
Why are you covered in sweat?

195
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:07,920
Am I?

196
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:09,720
She's embarrassed.

197
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:11,920
I just scolded her, Ms. Luo.

198
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:13,480
Tell your mother yourself.

199
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:16,360
Wasn't this problem wrong
because you were careless?

200
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:17,680
Yes.

201
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:18,960
I made a careless mistake.

202
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:19,760
Xiyu,

203
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:21,040
math is your weak subject.

204
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:23,200
Let He Lan teach you properly.

205
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:25,360
Remember to treat He Lan to lunch.

206
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:25,840
Okay?

207
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,240
You're too kind, Ms. Luo.

208
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:27,960
I really appreciate your kindness.

209
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:28,480
Mom,

210
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:29,600
I gotta hang up now.

211
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:30,800
We're disturbing the others.

212
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:31,720
Bye.

213
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:36,720
Good thing you reacted fast.

214
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:38,080
You two...

215
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:43,960
Xiyu,

216
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:46,320
you should consider applying
for the dance theater program.

217
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:47,920
I think you have great acting skills.

218
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:50,480
As for He Lan,

219
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,320
you could study directing

220
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:52,960
or stage design.

221
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:54,880
You have potential too.

222
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:56,920
Alright,

223
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:58,400
I'll head back first.

224
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,200
Goodbye, Ms. Lin.

225
00:09:59,200 --> 00:09:59,960
I'll leave after

226
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:01,280
applying medicine to He Lan.

227
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:02,080
Make it quick.

228
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:02,640
Okay.

229
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,720
First,

230
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:15,360
apply a wet gauze compress.

231
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,120
Then,

232
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:21,240
use iodine solution

233
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,440
to disinfect the wound.

234
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:28,320
Clean the wound area.

235
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:41,160
You actually inherited some
of your mom's genes.

236
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:43,680
If you didn't dance,

237
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:46,280
you'd definitely make a great doctor.

238
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:48,320
No way.

239
00:10:48,880 --> 00:10:51,160
Whenever my mom finishes
several surgeries

240
00:10:51,280 --> 00:10:52,760
or works a night shift,

241
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,000
the moment she gets home,

242
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:55,200
she always says,

243
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,000
"Anyone who talks people
into studying medicine

244
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:58,480
deserves to be struck by lightning."

245
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:00,880
But honestly,

246
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:02,880
being a doctor really is exhausting.

247
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:05,440
Actually,

248
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:07,440
what job isn't exhausting?

249
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:08,560
But

250
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:10,960
as long as you can stick with
what you love,

251
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:12,560
it's all worth it.

252
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:21,560
Why are you moving?

253
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:23,480
I have a question for you.

254
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:24,720
What is it?

255
00:11:30,400 --> 00:11:31,840
When will you turn eighteen?

256
00:11:33,360 --> 00:11:34,360
Why are you asking?

257
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:37,400
The gauze isn't finished yet.

258
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:38,560
Turn around.

259
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:41,680
Seriously.

260
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,000
It's wrapped too tight.

261
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:48,000
Then bear with it.

262
00:11:50,520 --> 00:11:51,240
Unbelievable.

263
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:53,400
You're still complaining
while I'm patching you up?

264
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:55,200
I'm satisfied. Of course I am.

265
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:27,320
♪I hide my racing heart without a sound♪

266
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:33,840
♪I close my eyes and pretend
the story's been reset♪

267
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:37,960
♪I steer clear of every path
that leads to you♪

268
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:41,120
♪Trying to outrun the storm
we're destined for♪

269
00:12:41,990 --> 00:12:44,080
♪I thought if I didn't hear, see,
or speak of you♪

270
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:47,640
♪I could cut every thread
that ties us together♪

271
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:53,760
♪Through the endless night,
I guard my only secret♪

272
00:12:55,470 --> 00:13:00,320
♪In this new cycle, I watch you
become innocent again♪

273
00:13:01,650 --> 00:13:03,780
♪I tried to erase the fire we once had♪

274
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:07,530
♪But I can't erase your name
carved into my bones♪

275
00:13:08,290 --> 00:13:10,470
♪The more I try to leave you behind♪

276
00:13:10,470 --> 00:13:14,440
♪The deeper I sink with no end in sight♪

277
00:13:14,730 --> 00:13:17,650
♪What if I stayed a little farther away♪

278
00:13:17,650 --> 00:13:20,720
♪Could I finally break free
from this cycle♪

279
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:23,280
♪What if I took things a little slower♪

280
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:27,120
♪Could I delay the moment
everything falls apart♪

281
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:31,310
♪Maybe if I retreat to the edge
of my dreams♪

282
00:13:31,310 --> 00:13:34,240
♪I could give you another future♪

283
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:40,720
♪A tomorrow where I no longer exist♪

284
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:43,140
♪Even if I never want to see you again♪

285
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:44,680
♪This nightmare still won't end♪

286
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:46,640
♪Even if it all plays out again♪

287
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:48,680
♪I'll still find my way back to you♪

288
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:52,730
♪Even if having you only leaves me
in your debt♪

289
00:13:52,730 --> 00:13:56,720
♪It's still better than
losing you forever♪
